      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`Qwen3VLConfig` and `Qwen3VLMoeConfig` document support for config objects as well as dictionaries, but their constructors only assign `text_config`/`vision_config` for dictionaries or `None`. Passing an existing sub-config leaves the corresponding attribute unset:\n\n```python\nfrom sglang.srt.configs.qwen3_vl import Qwen3VLConfig\n\ntext = Qwen3VLConfig.sub_configs[\"text_config\"](hidden_size=128)\nconfig = Qwen3VLConfig(text_config=text)\nconfig.text_config  # AttributeError before this fix\n```\n\n## Modifications\n\nPreserve supplied sub-config objects in both constructors. Dictionary conversion and defaults are unchanged. Add a registered CPU regression covering object/dictionary combinations, object identity, serialization and round trips for both families.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOn Linux/Python 3.12 with the pinned Transformers 5.19.0, using normal SGLang package imports:\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest test/registered/unit/configs/test_qwen3_vl_config.py -q\n```\n\nBefore: all six object-input subcases fail with `AttributeError`. After: one test and all six subcases pass. Other dependencies are inherited from the test environment; this is not a full official CI or model-inference result.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: config construction only, no inference-path or kernel change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Full pre-commit run: most applicable hooks pass, but Windows application control blocks the Ruff hook launchers; `python3` hook entrypoints are also unavailable. Pinned Ruff 0.15.1 lint/format and the three affected Python hook scripts were checked directly with native tools.\n- [x] Add registered CPU regression tests.\n- Documentation: the fix implements the existing documented input contract.\n- No model accuracy or speed claim.\n\nAI-assisted change; the regression was checked against both the original and fixed source through real package imports.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37954289681](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37954289681)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37954289129](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37954289129)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37954289682](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37954289682)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
